title: EmergencySeed_Start
tags:
---
<<wait_for_action pick_up_clay_jar>>
maya-didi: Yeh dekh. Clay jar. Ek hi kaam karta hai — bachata hai.
maya-didi: This one is different from the Save envelope. This is the vault.
<<player_choose>>
-> "What's the difference?"
    maya-didi: Save envelope is for goals. New phone. Diwali clothes.
    maya-didi: This jar is for emergencies. Hospital. Job gap. Roof leak.
    <<jump EmergencySeed_Why>>
-> "Why a jar? Why not the envelope?"
    maya-didi: Because envelopes open easy. Jars have to be broken.
    maya-didi: Friction is the feature. You will thank the friction later.
    <<jump EmergencySeed_Why>>
===

title: EmergencySeed_Why
tags:
---
maya-didi: Goal is six months of expenses. For you, around ₹50,000.
maya-didi: That is a mountain. We don't climb mountains. We climb stairs.
maya-didi: First stair — ₹500. Today. From the Save envelope.
<<player_choose>>
-> "Drop ₹500 into the jar."
    <<wait_for_action drop_into_jar 500>>
    <<jump EmergencySeed_Locked>>
-> "Only ₹500? That's nothing."
    maya-didi: ₹500 today is the proof that the jar exists.
    maya-didi: Proof matters more than amount. Start small. Stay started.
    <<wait_for_action drop_into_jar 500>>
    <<jump EmergencySeed_Locked>>
-> "Can I do ₹1,000?"
    maya-didi: Achha! Yes. But only if your Spend envelope still survives.
    <<wait_for_action drop_into_jar 1000>>
    <<set_flag emergency_seed_doubled>>
    <<jump EmergencySeed_Locked>>
===

title: EmergencySeed_Locked
tags:
---
<<wait_for_action close_jar_lid>>
maya-didi: Now the lock. First time, I do it. After this, it's yours.
<<wait_for_action lock_jar>>
maya-didi: One rule. To open this jar, you have to walk to me first.
maya-didi: Not because I will say no. Because the walk gives you ten minutes.
maya-didi: Ten minutes is enough to know — is this a real emergency?
<<player_choose>>
-> "What counts as a real emergency?"
    maya-didi: Hospital. Job loss. Family illness. Roof actually falling.
    maya-didi: Not — new phone. Not — friend's wedding. Not — sale on TV.
-> "What if I really need it for something else?"
    maya-didi: Then you walk to me. We talk. Maybe you do open it.
    maya-didi: But you'll know it cost you something. Not just the rupees.
<<continue>>
<<jump EmergencySeed_Pledge>>
===

title: EmergencySeed_Pledge
tags:
---
maya-didi: Last thing. Make a pledge. Every salary day — ₹500 into this jar.
maya-didi: Same as rent. Non-negotiable. Boring. Automatic.
<<player_choose>>
-> "₹500 every month. Pledged."
    <<set_flag emergency_seed_pledged>>
    maya-didi: In ten months — ₹5,000. In two years — ₹12,000.
    maya-didi: That is one job-gap month, fully covered. From a clay jar.
-> "Let me see how the first month goes."
    maya-didi: Theek hai. No pledge. But the jar is yours.
    maya-didi: Come back when you're ready to commit. The jar will wait.
    <<set_flag emergency_seed_tentative>>
<<continue>>
<<grant_mastery budgeting.emergency-seed 1>>
<<set_flag finished_emergency_seed>>
maya-didi: You have three envelopes and a jar. That is a budget.
maya-didi: Tomorrow — I have someone to introduce you to.
===
